<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The seven Big and Small gene tools sit only in Alpha Genes' gene tools category, instead of appearing in both
		that category and vanilla's miscellaneous items.

		How it works, because the Inherit="False" is easy to miss: Big and Small already puts these tools in
		AG_GeneTools, through BS_GeneToolBase, which carries that category behind its own Alpha Genes check. But that
		abstract parent inherits ItemsMisc from BS_SerumBase above it, so without this patch each tool resolves to both
		categories. Writing the list straight onto the seven tools with Inherit="False" cuts the inherited ItemsMisc
		entry, leaving the Alpha Genes category alone. Side effect worth knowing: the tools stop showing up under
		miscellaneous items in storage and bill filters.
		See also the Integrations mod, which re-parents the AG_GeneTools category itself from Manufactured to Items.

		Gating, which is why this is its own folder: the gene tools are not a Big and Small - Races def. Genes &amp; More
		defines them, inside a Conditional/AnyContentMod folder its own LoadFolders only loads when at least one Big and
		Small content mod is active. This folder mirrors that list exactly, which is wider than the six mods the
		original checked for. Alpha Genes is gated on the operation itself, since it owns the category.
		The mod gate sits on an <li> inside a sequence, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads MayRequire only on
		list elements, so an <Operation MayRequire="..."> node loads and applies unconditionally.

		Verified against Genes &amp; More 1.6: all seven tools exist, all inherit from BS_GeneToolBase, and none defines a
		thingCategories list of its own, so the add creates one rather than duplicating.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sarg.alphagenes">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>
							Defs/ThingDef[defName="BS_GeneDicombobulator" or defName="BS_GeneGeneIntegrator" or defName="BS_XenoCopy" or defName="BS_CreateXenogerm" or defName="BS_CreateArchiteXenogerm" or defName="BS_CreateArchiteXenogerm_Endo" or defName="BS_CreateXenogerm_Endo"]</xpath>
						<value>
							<thingCategories Inherit="False">
								<li>AG_GeneTools</li>
							</thingCategories>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
